Subject: [PATCH 13/26] docs: SETUP-PULL.md (GitHub setup, two-token model,
 native install, updates)

- How the pull model works, and why the build repository must be a
  PRIVATE repository filled by a push, not a fork (a fork of a public
  repo is public).
- Token decision: two fine-grained PATs, both limited to the one repo.
  The install/update token has Contents, Workflows and Secrets RW and is
  used interactively, not stored. The runtime token has Actions RW and
  Metadata R and lives in /etc/rdgen/rdgen.env. Rationale: code
  execution in the web process then cannot push a workflow that dumps
  the repo's signing secrets or runs arbitrary code on your billing.
- Required and optional repository secrets. GENURL is gone.
- Native install steps for Alpine 3.24 and Debian 13 (Django 5.2 from
  trixie-backports), nginx LAN port or sub-path, CortenDesk link.
- Update contract: what rdgen-github-bootstrap update does, and the
  deploy order the LXC update script should follow.
- What the patch series fixes and what it cannot, plus the JSON API.

